* Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE).
*
* jBASE reaches C with DEFC, which declares a FUNCTION -- so the engine's entry
* points cannot be CALLed directly the way MVX's can.  This is the one line of
* glue that fixes that: a subroutine with MVX's exact signature, wrapping the
* DEFC function.  With it, every handler's engine arm works here unchanged,
* which is why the guard can be $IFDEF ENGINE rather than a second copy of the
* body under $IFDEF JBASE (mv_git#114).
      SUBROUTINE GITSTATUS(REPO, ANS)
      DEFC VAR JBGITSTATUS(VAR, VAR)
      ANS = ""
      X = JBGITSTATUS(REPO, ANS)
      RETURN
